  "oracle_fix": "The leading-packet frame branch of KD-HLS-2 never required the frames it covers to be unpresented. With the branch limited to audio and to frames before the source's first presented packet ('new_strict_oracle'), ae16bb7c7192 and fcb01fd0c565 fail: their 13 and 16 differing frames are presented audio. A binary with no audio lead (AUDIO_LEAD 0) is covered by the first oracle and fails with the strict one.",
  "cause": {
   "finding": "ffmpeg applies the audio rendition's edit media time (37824) counting from its first sample's decode time (tfdt 15360) instead of from media time 0, so it drops 15360 samples (0.348 s) of presented audio; the rendition is as ISO/IEC 14496-12 8.6.6 reads it.",
   "test": "fcb01fd0c565: the audio rendition with its init's elst media time set to 37824 - 15360 decodes in the pinned ffmpeg to the source's 233 frames, hash for hash"
  }
